# Open in VS Code with the REST Client extension (humao.rest-client).
# Click "Send Request" above any block to run it.
#
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  If the response panel only shows the raw text and no JSON tab,
#  your REST Client is too old. Update it:
#    Ctrl+Shift+P → "Extensions: Show Enabled Extensions" → REST Client → Update
#  Or just use the right-click menu on the response body → "Format JSON".
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# Vim tip: if you want pretty JSON in vim, run:
#   :%!python -m json.tool     (if you have python)
#   :%!jq .                    (if you have jq)
#
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  If the PATCH examples 404, the placeholder UUID doesn't exist in
#  your DB. Two fixes (pick one):
#
#    (a) Right-click → "Send All Requests in File" — runs CREATE
#        first, then the chained PATCH picks up the real id.
#        Requires REST Client >= 0.24 (2021+) for response chaining.
#
#    (b) Run the CREATE request (#1) first, copy the "data1" UUID
#        from the response, paste it over the placeholder below.
#        Works in any version of REST Client.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

@host = http://localhost:8080

### Health check
GET {{host}}/healthz

### 1) Create a product — the response is the source of the id for #2-#5
POST {{host}}/product
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Espresso Beans 1kg",
  "description": "Single-origin Ethiopian roast",
  "sale_price": 24.50,
  "price": 29.90
}

### 2) Create a minimal product (no optional fields) — for testing the "patch with nulls" case
POST {{host}}/product
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Plain Mug",
  "price": 9.99
}

### 3) List all products (sanity check the DB has data)
GET {{host}}/product

### 4) Get by id — replace PASTE-UUID-HERE with a real one (copy from #1 or #3)
GET {{host}}/product/PASTE-UUID-HERE

### 5) Patch by id — change only the price
PATCH {{host}}/product/PASTE-UUID-HERE
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "price": 31.50
}

### 6) Patch by id — null out description and sale_price (explicit clear)
PATCH {{host}}/product/PASTE-UUID-HERE
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": null,
  "sale_price": null
}

### 7) Patch by id — invalid (negative price), expect 422 INVALID_PRICE
PATCH {{host}}/product/PASTE-UUID-HERE
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "price": -1
}

### 8) Patch a non-existent id, expect 404 PRODUCT_NOT_FOUND
PATCH {{host}}/product/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "price": 1
}
